% ============================================================================
% wind-scale.query.adj — a worked recall over the meteorology wind-scale library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is a force-6 wind
% called?": it states no weather fact — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `beaufort_force_name` rows and returns the name + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the name hurricane,
% recall the force number that has it — 12). Beaufort force 13 is off the top of
% the scale, so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% name.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli wind-scale.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "wind-scale.adj"

? beaufort_force_name(0, $Name)    % expect calm
? beaufort_force_name(6, $Name)    % expect strong_breeze
? beaufort_force_name(12, $Name)   % expect hurricane
? beaufort_force_name($F, hurricane) % expect 12 — reverse recall
? beaufort_force_name(13, $Name)   % expect abstain — 13 is off the top of the scale
